            <ArticleTitle>A clinical evaluation of one and two-appointment root canal therapy using calcium hydroxide.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A clinical study using vital maxillary central incisors was performed to evaluate the incidence of postoperative pain after root canal treatment in one- or two-appointments using a calcium hydroxide-containing root canal sealer. No differences were observed between the two groups.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
